    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0bb57e5b002226cd02a95601ab9948bbdcb01380281be779b4da8f2ec13995b2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The three coefficient designs exchange exact local cancellation for simpler arithmetic structure and then for stronger truncation regularity. Two terminal corrections added to Moebius-weighted interior coefficients solve the finite triangular system exactly; removing those corrections gives the natural mu(q)/q family but exposes a moving low-mode norm governed by two simultaneous summatory-Moebius conditions; multiplying by q^{-epsilon_n} introduces a vanishing fixed-coordinate bias while making the omitted Dirichlet tails directly controllable. Smoothing repairs tail estimation, not the remaining uniform Hilbert-norm domination problem.",
