    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7cdada20c28f5393ec8163efb2646af94d6c807f7b5568f60fd4a2288ece5a0b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The symmetry conditions defining HP do more than shrink the ambient Hilbert space: folding the weighted norm and multiplying by the sine factor identify HP isometrically with the odd-cosine Fourier sector, where the adjacent sine differences E_p are a complete orthonormal basis. The coefficient-correction argument then shows that replacing the ambient fractional-part generators by e_q={qt}-{t} preserves the RH closure criterion, and the coordinate formula <E_p,e_q>=log q-sum_{p/q<=k<p}1/k turns that closure problem into convergence of explicit arithmetic coordinate sequences.",
